// GroundAoe's strike is a single instantaneous burst (buildup -> telegraph
// delay -> one explosion at the locked point -> recover; see
// common/src/states/ground_aoe.rs), not a lingering hazard zone. The sheet's
// "the fire lingers, burning anyone who enters or remains within it" rider is
// dropped for v1 -- no persistent-zone primitive exists for GroundAoe (same
// simplification already accepted for axiomancy/dark_star.ron and
// axiomancy/gravity_sinkhole.ron, both of which also describe a
// lingering/zone effect in their sheet notes and ship as one-shot bursts).
// Also note: GroundAoe's damage strike is hardcoded to `DamageKind::Energy`
// (see the same file) -- the sheet's Fire damage_type is flavor-only here,
// not mechanically expressible via GroundAoe; every existing GroundAoe spell
// (bloodboil, dark_star, gravity_sinkhole) is Energy-kind regardless of its
// own elemental flavor, so this isn't a new gap, just an existing one.
GroundAoe(
    energy_cost: 0.0,
    buildup_duration: 0.6,
    delay: 0.4,
    recover_duration: 0.4,
    max_range: 18.0,
    radius: 3.0,
    min_falloff: 0.4,
    damage: 14.0,
    poise: 5.0,
    knockback: (strength: 0.0, direction: Away),
    dodgeable: Roll,
    reagent: Some(Red),
    rooted_cast: false,
    meta: (school: Some(Conjuration), source: Some(Arcane)),
)
